# Update docs after each step

Do not batch documentation until the end of a task. After **each** completed step (new file, behavior change, API/type change, UI change, rename, or delete), update **every** doc that the change makes stale. Then continue.

## What to touch

- Colocated `README.md` in the folder you changed (`components/Lists/README.md`, `lib/README.md`, …) — architecture trees, file lists, and behavior notes.
- Parent folder READMEs if the change is visible there (`components/README.md`, `app/README.md`).
- Root `README.md` for user-facing features, overview claims, or the repository map.
- `docs/README.md` if the docs index itself changed.
- `docs/SPEC_MAPPING.md` when a spec’d feature moves between missing / partial / implemented.
- `docs/tree.md` and `docs/tree.txt` when files or folders are added, moved, or removed (`npm run tree`).
- `docs/screenshots/` PNG + `.txt` sidecars when a captured view’s UI or copy changed (`npm run capture-screenshots` while the app is running). See `docs/screenshots/README.md`.

Skip docs that are unrelated. Do not invent entries in `docs/BRAIN2_FEATURE_IDEAS.md` unless the work was specifically about that idea bank.

## How

Match the existing README style (purpose sentence, file tree, short behavior notes). Fully rewrite stale sections; do not leave old names, paths, or “coming soon” that are now shipped.

When the work departs from what was asked, or from the plan already written in the docs — a new idea, a renamed concept, a dropped piece of scope, a different default, a metric that was not in the catalog, a layout decision that contradicts an earlier note — update the docs that describe that feature **in the same step**. Say what was decided and why, not only which files changed. Do not leave the old plan stating the abandoned behavior.

```text
❌ BAD: land the Lists checkbox filter, then “docs at the end”
✅ GOOD: ship the filter, then in the same step update
   components/Lists/README.md (tree + behavior) and any screenshot write-up
   for the Lists content view
❌ BAD: ship a new default and leave the plan describing the old one
✅ GOOD: rewrite that note in the same step — the decision, and why
```
